            "text": "...",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "(Continue)",
                "nextNodeId": "return_visit",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_SET",
                    "target": "kael_met",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "(Continue)",
                "nextNodeId": "first_meeting",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "kael_met",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "first_meeting": {
            "id": "first_meeting",
            "text": "You're awake! Thank the tides. I found you tangled in the kelp three dawns ago, half-drowned and burning with fever. That scar on your chest... it was glowing when I pulled you from the surf.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What is this place?",
                "nextNodeId": "about_island"
              },
              {
                "label": "Tell me about this scar.",
                "nextNodeId": "about_scar"
              },
              {
                "label": "I need supplies.",
                "nextNodeId": "point_moonhaven"
              },
              {
                "label": "Thank you for saving me. Farewell.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "about_scar": {
            "id": "about_scar",
            "text": "That mark on your chest... I've seen it only once before, on a woman who came from the sea thirty years ago. She founded Moonhaven before vanishing into the dungeon beneath the island. They say she went to level 50. No one goes to level 50 and comes back.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What happened to her?",
                "nextNodeId": "deep_lore",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "PLAYER_LEVEL",
                    "amount": 5,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "Tell me about the island.",
                "nextNodeId": "about_island"
              },
              {
                "label": "Where can I find supplies?",
                "nextNodeId": "point_moonhaven"
              },
              {
                "label": "I see. Farewell.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "deep_lore": {
            "id": "deep_lore",
            "text": "Her name was Seraphine. She spoke of a 'heart' deep beneath the island -- something ancient, something that called to her through the scar. The deeper she went, the more the dungeon changed around her. After level 10, the walls themselves begin to breathe. After level 30... well, the few who returned that far spoke only in riddles before they died.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll find what she couldn't.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              },
              {
                "label": "That's... unsettling. Tell me about the island.",
                "nextNodeId": "about_island"
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "heard_deep_lore",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "about_island": {
            "id": "about_island",
            "text": "This is Lirandel -- a mysterious island with a massive dungeon beneath it. Beautiful on the surface, but dark things stir below. Monsters have been crawling up from the depths lately. The Corrupted Crabs along the shore are just the beginning. I've seen shadows in the treeline that weren't there last season.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Where should I go first?",
                "nextNodeId": "point_moonhaven"
              },
              {
                "label": "Tell me about the scar on my chest.",
                "nextNodeId": "about_scar"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'll be careful. Farewell.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "point_moonhaven": {
            "id": "point_moonhaven",
            "text": "Head east along the shore -- you'll find Moonhaven, the only settlement on Lirandel. It's small but sturdy. There's an inn where you can rest and recover, a shop for supplies, and a healer if those crabs get the better of you. Tell them Kael sent you.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What about the dungeon entrance?",
                "nextNodeId": "dungeon_warning"
              },
              {
                "label": "Thank you, Kael.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "dungeon_warning": {
            "id": "dungeon_warning",
            "text": "The locals call it the Dreamwake Caverns -- the entrance is beyond Moonhaven, deeper inland. But don't rush in unprepared -- even the first level will test you. Stock up on potions, learn what spells you can, and for the love of the tides, don't go below level 5 until you're sure of yourself.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll be careful.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              },
              {
                "label": "Sounds like you speak from experience.",
                "nextNodeId": "kael_backstory"
              }
            ]
          },
          "kael_backstory": {
            "id": "kael_backstory",
            "text": "I was an adventurer once, decades ago. Made it to level 12 before a Flame Wraith took my sword arm. Now I comb these beaches, watching for shipwrecks and lost souls like yourself. The island provides, if you respect it.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "You're braver than you let on.",
                "nextNodeId": "first_farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "first_farewell": {
            "id": "first_farewell",
            "text": "Here -- take this. It's not much, but it might save your life out there. The crabs are thickest near the water's edge. Stay sharp, traveler.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Thank you, Kael. I won't forget this."
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "healing_potion",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "kael_met",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Kael presses a healing potion into your hand.",
                "value": "LOOT",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "return_visit": {
            "id": "return_visit",
            "text": "Back again? The dungeon hasn't claimed you yet -- that's a good sign. The beaches are a little quieter since you arrived.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I dealt with the crabs.",
                "nextNodeId": "crabs_done",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_COMPLETE",
                    "target": "rising_tide",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "Any news from the island?",
                "nextNodeId": "return_news"
              },
              {
                "label": "Tell me about the scar again.",
                "nextNodeId": "about_scar"
              },
              {
                "label": "What do you know about the deeper levels?",
                "nextNodeId": "deep_lore",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "PLAYER_LEVEL",
                    "amount": 5,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "Just passing through. Farewell."
              }
            ]
          },
          "crabs_done": {
            "id": "crabs_done",
            "text": "You dealt with the Corrupted Crabs! Moonhaven is safer thanks to you. The fishermen can work the shore again without looking over their shoulders. You've earned their respect -- and mine.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What's next for me?",
                "nextNodeId": "return_news"
              },
              {
                "label": "Just doing what needs to be done. Farewell."
              }
            ]
          },
          "return_news": {
            "id": "return_news",
            "text": "I've been hearing strange sounds from the north -- grinding stone, like the island itself is shifting. And the fishermen say the tides have been wrong lately. Whatever lives at the bottom of that dungeon, it's getting restless.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll look into it."
              },
              {
                "label": "Anything else?",
                "nextNodeId": "return_advice"
              }
            ]
          },
          "return_advice": {
            "id": "return_advice",
            "text": "Just... be careful with the altars down there. Some grant blessings, others take more than they give. And if you find a glowing cube, think twice before touching it. The dungeon has a way of testing those who disturb its treasures.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Good advice. Thank you, Kael."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 12,
      "y": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_lirandel_seagull",
      "name": "Scraggly Seagull",
      "spriteName": "npcs/seagull",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "SQUAAAAWK! Crabs! DANGER! SQUAAAAWK! ...Also fish. Mostly fish.",
      "questId": "",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "x": 10,
      "y": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_shipwreck_sailor",
      "name": "Ghostly Sailor",
      "spriteName": "npcs/pirate",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "Arrgh... these waters claimed me fifty years past...",
      "questId": "",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start_router",
        "nodes": {
          "start_router": {
            "id": "start_router",
            "text": "...",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "(Approach)",
                "nextNodeId": "first_visit",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "sailor_rewarded",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "(Approach)",
                "nextNodeId": "return_visit",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_SET",
                    "target": "sailor_rewarded",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "first_visit": {
            "id": "first_visit",
            "text": "You can see me? Ha... it's been decades since anyone wandered into this cove.\n\nMy ship was the Moonstrider. She broke apart on that reef fifty years ago — storm came out of nowhere, no warning at all. Everything of value went down with her.\n\nEverything except the captain's chest I hid in the shallows before she sank. Take it, friend. I've no use for gold where I'm drifting.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Thank you, sailor. What happened to your crew?",
                "nextNodeId": "crew_story"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'll take it. Thank you.",
                "nextNodeId": "give_loot"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "crew_story": {
            "id": "crew_story",
            "text": "Most made it to shore. Good lads, all of them. Brynar became a fisherman in Moonhaven — you might have seen him. I stayed behind to try to right the ship. Foolish.\n\nTake the chest. Consider it an old sailor's apology for making his family worry.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I will. Rest well, sailor.",
                "nextNodeId": "give_loot"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "give_loot": {
            "id": "give_loot",
            "text": "Go on now. And keep her off the rocks.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Farewell."
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_GOLD",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 12
              },
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "rusty_sword",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "sailor_rewarded",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Found the captain's chest: 12 gold and a Rusty Sword.",
                "value": "LOOT",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "return_visit": {
            "id": "return_visit",
            "text": "Still out here, are you? These waters suit me now. I hope that sword hasn't rusted through entirely.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Safe sailing, sailor."
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 45,
      "y": 82
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_1774048273940",
      "name": "Eldorf the Ranger",
      "spriteName": "npcs/ranger",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "Beware this place!  You will surely die here!",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "x": 55,
      "y": 48,
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "greeting",
        "nodes": {
          "greeting": {
            "id": "greeting",
            "text": "Beware this place. You will surely die here.\n[He does not look up from the boot he is mending. After a moment he seems to hear himself.]\n...That is what I say. I have said it to everyone who has come up this road for eleven years and I have never once meant it as much as it sounds.\nIt is a moor. Moors kill people who are stupid on them. Do not be stupid on it and you will be fine.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What is there to be stupid about?",
                "nextNodeId": "eldorf_moor",
                "conditions": []
              },
              {
                "label": "Eleven years out here alone?",
                "nextNodeId": "eldorf_years",
                "conditions": []
              },
              {
                "label": "I will be careful.",
                "nextNodeId": "eldorf_bye",
                "conditions": []
              },
              {
                "label": "What is up at the old standing stones?",
                "nextNodeId": "eldorf_stones",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_ACTIVE",
                    "target": "the_standing_stones",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "eldorf_told_stones",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "eldorf_moor": {
            "id": "eldorf_moor",
            "text": "Wolves, weather, and the ravine, in that order and none of them close.\nThe wolves have gone odd this last year — packing up wrong, denning where there is no cover. Wolfie in Moonhaven has a theory about it and Wolfie has a theory about everything, so I do not listen, and I probably should.\nThe weather comes off the sea in under an hour. And the ravine has no bottom that I have found and I have thrown things.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Thank you.",
                "nextNodeId": "eldorf_bye",
                "conditions": []
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "eldorf_years": {
            "id": "eldorf_years",
            "text": "Twelve in spring. I came up to get away from a town and I have got away from it very thoroughly.\n[He turns the boot over.] It suits me. I mend what I have got, I walk the same ground, and every so often somebody comes up the road and I frighten them and then feel foolish about it. That is a life. I have had worse ones.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Fair enough.",
                "nextNodeId": "eldorf_bye",
                "conditions": []
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "eldorf_bye": {
            "id": "eldorf_bye",
            "text": "Keep to the road until the second cairn. After that there is no road, and that is not a warning, it is just true.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "eldorf_stones": {
            "id": "eldorf_stones",
            "text": "The markers? Nothing. Rocks.\n[He goes back to the boot he is mending. You wait. He does not like being waited at.]\n...They are warm. That is all. It is not interesting; it is a rock thing, rocks hold the sun.\n[You keep waiting.]\nIn winter. All right. In winter, and under cloud, and I have sat on one in a snowstorm to eat my dinner and the snow came off it in a ring three paces wide and I did not think about it once in eleven years until a stranger stood there and made me.\nAnd the wolves sit round it facing in. I have always assumed they liked the warm. That is what I assumed. That is a perfectly sensible thing to have assumed.\n[He puts the boot down.] Tell Wolfie. Tell him from me that I am not going back up there for a while.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "eldorf_told_stones",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_mazzy_adventurer",
      "name": "Mazzy",
      "spriteName": "npcs/child",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "...",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start_router",
        "nodes": {
          "start_router": {
            "id": "start_router",
            "text": "...",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "(Approach)",
                "nextNodeId": "post_quest",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_COMPLETE",
                    "target": "mazzys_ring",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "(Approach)",
                "nextNodeId": "return_visit",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_ACTIVE",
                    "target": "mazzys_ring",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "(Approach)",
                "nextNodeId": "first_meeting",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "mazzy_met",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "first_meeting": {
            "id": "first_meeting",
            "text": "You found me... *cough*... I thought I'd die alone out here.\n\nThe dungeon took everything. My sword, my armor, my pride. But not this ring. It was my mother's -- she gave it to me before I left home.\n\nPlease... take it to my brother Frederick in Mooncrest. East, past the mountains. Tell him I'm sorry I didn't come home.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll find him. I promise.",
                "nextNodeId": "accepted"
              },
              {
                "label": "I can't right now.",
                "nextNodeId": "decline"
              }
            ]
          },
          "accepted": {
            "id": "accepted",
            "text": "Thank you... *cough*... Frederick will know it's real when he sees the inscription. \"Until the tides return.\" That was what mother always said.\n\nGo now. Don't waste time on a fool who went too deep.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Rest easy, Mazzy. I'll deliver it."
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_QUEST",
                "target": "mazzys_ring",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "ring_protection_5",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "mazzy_met",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Mazzy presses a ring into your hand. It glows faintly.",
                "value": "LOOT",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "decline": {
            "id": "decline",
            "text": "I understand... *cough*... if you change your mind, I'll be here. I'm not going anywhere.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll come back."
              }
            ]
          },
          "return_visit": {
            "id": "return_visit",
            "text": "You came back... have you found Frederick yet? Mooncrest... east past the mountains. Please hurry.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'm on my way. Hold on, Mazzy."
              }
            ]
          },
          "post_quest": {
            "id": "post_quest",
            "text": "You found him... *cough*... I can see it in your eyes. Frederick has the ring.\n\nThank you. Truly. Knowing he has it... that's enough. That's more than I deserve.\n\nYou're braver than I ever was, traveler. The island could use someone like you.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Take care of yourself, Mazzy."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 62,
      "y": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_ruins_hermit",
      "name": "Verath the Blind",
      "spriteName": "npcs/oracle",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "Who enters these ruins? I sense... the mark of the scar upon you.",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "You found your way past the gate... good. Few bother with these old ruins. But I have been waiting.\n\nI am Verath. I lost my sight in the Dreamwake Caverns long ago, but what I saw on the third level... that I will never forget.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What did you see on level 3?",
                "nextNodeId": "boss_info"
              },
              {
                "label": "How did you lose your sight?",
                "nextNodeId": "backstory"
              },
              {
                "label": "Rook of Mooncrest is asking after a Veil Shard.",
                "nextNodeId": "veil_give",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_ACTIVE",
                    "target": "shadow_errand",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "verath_gave_veil",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "I should go.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "boss_info": {
            "id": "boss_info",
            "text": "On the third level there is an altar unlike the others. It pulses with a sickly light. When I touched it, something rose from the stone -- a guardian, ancient and terrible.\n\nIt feeds on the corruption of the shrines. If you have been destroying them as part of your purge, the guardian will be weaker. But if the shrines still stand... it will draw power from every one of them.\n\nDestroy the shrines on the upper levels BEFORE you face the altar on level 3. That is the only advice I can give you.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Is there anything else I should know?",
                "nextNodeId": "boss_detail"
              },
              {
                "label": "Thank you, Verath.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "boss_detail": {
            "id": "boss_detail",
            "text": "The guardian strikes with waves of corruption -- a dark energy that saps your strength. Healing spells and potions are your lifeline. And when it offers you a choice... choose carefully.\n\nThe gods are watching. Lirandel and Pyralis both have an interest in what happens at that altar. Your decision will shape their favor toward you.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I will remember. Thank you.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "backstory": {
            "id": "backstory",
            "text": "I was a scholar once, studying the caverns when they were merely strange, not yet corrupted. I reached the third level and found the altar. I was foolish -- I touched it without preparation, without having cleared the shrines.\n\nThe guardian nearly killed me. The blast of corruption took my eyes. I crawled back to the surface and have lived in these ruins ever since, warning those brave enough to seek me out.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What about the altar on level 3?",
                "nextNodeId": "boss_info"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'm sorry. Thank you for the warning.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ]
          },
          "farewell": {
            "id": "farewell",
            "text": "Go carefully, traveler. The Dreamwake Caverns do not forgive the unprepared. And remember -- clear the shrines before you face the third level.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Farewell, Verath."
              }
            ]
          },
          "veil_give": {
            "id": "veil_give",
            "text": "Rook. [The blind man smiles at a point somewhere past your shoulder, which is where he keeps everything.] Of course Rook.\nYes. I have one. I brought it up out of the Dreamwake in the same hour I lost my eyes, and I have kept it thirty years because I could never decide whether it was a relic or a wound.\nHere is what it is. There is a veil, and the gods see through it, and everything on the other side of it is visible to them and accounted for and — this is the part nobody says out loud — owned.\nThe shard is a hole in that. A splinter of not-being-seen.\n[He holds it out, and he is very precise about where your hand is, for a blind man.]\nWhich, I would guess, is why it has been humming since you walked up the path. It has met a bigger one. It has met you.\nTake it to Rook. He will sell it to somebody, and it will not matter, because you are the one who is a hole in the veil and there is nothing anybody can do about that with money.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "veil_shard",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "verath_gave_veil",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Verath presses a Veil Shard into your hand. It hums against the scar.",
                "value": "GOOD",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
